{"abstract":"This proposed rule would amend the Bureau of Industry and Security's (BIS) Defense Priorities and Allocations System (DPAS) regulation by providing administrative changes to well-established standards and procedures. This proposed rule would: clarify existing standards and procedures by which BIS may provide Special Priorities Assistance (SPA); revise Schedule I to provide transparency and differentiation between other departments' priorities jurisdiction and the Department of Commerce's jurisdiction; and provide technical edits to reflect certain non-substantive updates since the DPAS regulation was last amended in 2014, including providing updated contact information, legal citations, and definitions.","action":"Proposed rule.","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF COMMERCE","name":"Commerce Department","id":54,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/commerce-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/54","parent_id":null,"slug":"commerce-department"},{"raw_name":"Bureau of Industry and Security","name":"Industry and Security Bureau","id":241,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/industry-and-security-bureau","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/241","parent_id":54,"slug":"industry-and-security-bureau"}],"body_html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/html/2024/02/07/2024-01930.html","cfr_references":[{"chapter":null,"citation_url":null,"part":"700","title":15}],"citation":"89 FR 8363","comment_url":null,"comments_close_on":"2024-03-08","correction_of":null,"corrections":[],"dates":"Comments on this proposed rule must be received by BIS by no later than March 8, 2024.","disposition_notes":null,"docket_ids":["Docket No. 240108-0002"],"dockets":[{"supporting_documents":[],"agency_name":"BIS","documents":[{"comment_count":0,"comment_start_date":"2024-02-07","updated_at":"2024-03-09T00:08:36.073-05:00","comment_url":"https://www.regulations.gov/commenton/BIS-2024-0